# Controls what `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# This is a separate layer from .dockerignore: this file decides what leaves
# your machine, .dockerignore decides what lands in the image. Anything the
# build needs must survive BOTH — so Dockerfile, .dockerignore, backend/ and
# frontend/ are deliberately never excluded here.
#
# Note: the presence of this file disables gcloud's fallback of deriving
# exclusions from .gitignore, so every rule below is stated explicitly.

# Secrets — must never be uploaded (Cloud Run injects these at runtime)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
frontend/firebase-config.js

# Version control & CI (not part of the build context)
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Python virtualenvs & caches
.venv/
venv/
env/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Dev-only tooling — the production image installs requirements.txt only
backend/tests
backend/requirements-dev.txt

# Firebase deploy config & cache (used by `firebase deploy`, not by the container)
.firebase/
.firebaserc
firebase.json
firestore.rules
*firebase-debug.log

# Local notes, personal tooling & non-runtime assets (submission-assets alone is ~110 MB of video)
.claude/
BRIEF.md
IDEAS.md
scratch/
submission-assets/
reference/

# OS junk
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
